<Base
  title="The Names Genetic Genealogy Gave Back | Cassian Creed"
  description="Forensic genetic genealogy is known for naming suspects, but its quietest work restores identities to the unidentified dead. Five cases — Marcia King, Renee Nilsson, Gail Johnson, Margaret Fetterolf, and Joseph Serrao — where DNA and family-tree research gave a name back."
